{{also|Auch}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|goh|ouh}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*auk}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|ook||also}}, {{cog|fy|ek||also, too}}, {{cog|lb|och||also}}, {{cog|sv|och||and}}, {{cog|is|og||and}}, and archaic {{cog|en|eke||also}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/aʊ̯x/}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|de|/aʊ̯/}} {{a|chiefly southern Germany and Austria; also in the northern half in some positions, e.g. before ''{{l|de|nicht}}''}}
* {{audio|de|De-auch.ogg|audio}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[also]]; [[too]]; [[as well]] {{gloss|in addition to whatever or whoever has previously been listed}}
#: {{syn|de|ebenfalls|ebenso}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich will '''auch''' ein Eis.|''Stress on “auch”:'' I '''too''' want icecream.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich will '''auch''' ein Eis.|''Stress on “Eis”:'' I want icecream, '''too'''.}}
# {{ngd|Used for emphasis.}}
## {{ngd|To confirm a preceding statement by someone else}}: [[really]], [[actually]], [[indeed]], [[in fact]]
##: {{uxi|de|Ich will '''auch''' ein Eis.|''Stress on “will”:'' I '''do indeed''' want icecream.}}
##: {{uxi|de|Das ist '''auch''' so.|''Stress on “ist”:'' It '''really''' is like that.}}
##: {{ux|de|Du solltest zur Polizei gehen. ― Mach ich '''auch'''.|You should go to the police. ― I will.}}
## {{ngd|To ask for confirmation of something one considers necessary.}}
##: {{ux|de|Hast du das Licht '''auch''' ausgemacht?|Did you make sure to turn off the light?}}
## {{ngd|To imply that something is unreasonable.}}
##: {{ux|de|Du bist '''auch''' witzig... Wie soll ich das denn ohne Auto alles schaffen?!|You’re '''oh so''' ingenious... How am I supposed to get all of this done without the car?!}}
##: {{ux|de|Warum müssen die '''auch''' alle ihren Müll hier abladen!|Why do they all have to dump their rubbish here!}}
# [[even]] ({{n-g|implying an extreme example in the case mentioned, as compared to the implied reality}})
#: {{syn|de|sogar|selbst}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Auch''' wenn das stimmt, ist es noch kein endgültiger Beweis.|'''Even''' if this is true, it is no definite proof.}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Auch''' ein Professor schreibt schon mal was falsch.|'''Even''' a professor may misspell something at times.}}
# [[ever]] {{n-g|as in [[whatever]], [[whenever]], [[however]], etc.}}
#: {{ux|de|Was du '''auch''' tust, es wird immer einer besser sein.|What'''ever''' you do, someone will always do it better.}}

===Interjection===
{{head|de|interjection}}

# {{ngd|in answering a yes-no question, used to express that the thing asked about covers part of the truth but not all of it}}; “[[yes]], and [[more]]”
#: {{ux|de|Ach, du bist Bauingenieur. Dann baust du Brücken? — '''Auch.'''|Oh, you’re a construction engineer. So you build bridges? — '''Yeah. And other things, too.'''}}

